# Cost telemetry sidecar — invariants

## Why this rule exists

The 10-stage pipeline (Planner → Discovery → Retriever → Reasoner →
Skeptic → Synthesizer → Verifier → Report Generator → Revision Workflow
→ Epistemic Persistence) makes per-report unit economics impossible to
estimate from logs alone. Admin needs an exact `$X.XX` per report so we
can: (a) tune the V2 reasoner-class defaults toward the cheapest model
that still passes the forbidden-defaults regression, (b) cap reports
that exceed budget, (c) price Sovereign deals against real cost rather
than guesses, and (d) detect bottleneck agents (the Skeptic running
twice in a recovery loop, a verifier eating 4× budget).

This rule exists so the telemetry path itself cannot become the next
bug-fountain — the same pattern that produced 22 PR #36–#40 reviewer
findings is exactly the shape this code could take: async writes,
multi-writer races, deploy-skew, fallback UPDATEs that drop fields.

## Invariants

### I-1. Single instrumentation point

All token/duration/cost telemetry emission goes through **`callRoleModel`
in `openrouter/openrouterService.ts`**, after a successful call (primary
or fallback). Do NOT add `emitCallTelemetry` calls anywhere else
(orchestrator, discovery, revision, generator, extractors). Every LLM
call site already routes through `callRoleModel`; per Cursor rule 17,
ripple-and-grep confirms no exceptions exist.

If you add a new pathway that calls an LLM **without** going through
`callRoleModel`, you must either:

1. Route it through `callRoleModel` (preferred — gets fallback, model
   policy, BYOK forwarding, telemetry for free), or
2. Call `emitCallTelemetry` directly and write a regression test that
   asserts the new pathway produces an `agent_executions` row.

### I-2. Run scope is set by the orchestrator, never by `callRoleModel`

`runScope.run({ runId, userId?, orgId?, reportId?, phaseOverride? }, fn)`
is wrapped around the body of:

- `runResearchJob` in `researchOrchestrator.ts` (public entry; inner body
  is `runResearchJobInner` — do not call the inner function directly)
- `runDiscoveryOrchestrator` in `discoveryOrchestrator.ts` (often nested;
  inner scope shadows outer — spread parent ids into the inner ctx)
- `createReportRevision` in `reportRevisionService.ts`
- `generateIterativeReport` in `reportGenerator.ts` (called from the
  orchestrator — inherits scope; do not re-wrap)

After a successful pipeline completion, `researchOrchestrator` sets
`research_runs.report_id` and calls **`patchAgentExecutionsReportIdForRun`**
so existing `agent_executions` rows for that run get `report_id` backfilled
(scope was opened before the report id existed).

`callRoleModel` reads the current scope via `runScope.current()`. If
there is no scope (test harness, ad-hoc admin script), the emission is
tagged `run_id=NULL` and written to `agent_executions` with
`run_id IS NULL` — this is intentional and lets us track unattributed
calls. Do not throw when scope is missing.

### I-3. Writes are best-effort and non-blocking

`emitCallTelemetry` is `void` and `.catch(...)` swallows errors. A
telemetry DB outage **must not** fail a research run. The orchestrator's
existing `model_log` JSONB column remains the primary source of truth;
`agent_executions` is the analytics-optimized denormalization.

If you ever change `emitCallTelemetry` to throw or to `await` in the
critical path, you have created a new failure mode for completing
reports. Don't.

### I-4. Idempotency key prevents double-counting on retry/fallback

The unique key is:

`idempotency_key = sha256(run_id || role || call_purpose || started_at_ms || model || telemetry_invocation_id)`.

`callRoleModel` generates one **`telemetryInvocationId`** (UUID) per
invocation and passes it to both the primary and fallback `emitCallTelemetry`
calls, so primary+fallback still produce **two** rows (different `model`).

Parallel `callRoleModel` calls (e.g. `Promise.all`) get distinct invocation
ids so rows never collide on `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` when wall-clock
`started_at_ms` matches.

`ON CONFLICT (idempotency_key) DO NOTHING` is mandatory in the INSERT.

### I-5. Pricing is a configuration table, not hardcoded

`model_pricing` is a DB table seeded by the migration. Provider price
changes are an admin UPDATE on that table, never a code change. The
pricing catalog code reads pricing once per process start with a
60-second TTL refresh — pricing changes do not require a redeploy.

Models not present in `model_pricing` resolve to `(0, 0)` and the row
is logged at `WARN` level with model id. Cost shows as `$0.00` but the
row still exists with tokens — operators see "we used model X 14,200
tokens but no price configured" and can backfill.

### I-6. Deploy-skew tolerance (Cursor rule 13)

Until migration 030 has applied, `emitCallTelemetry` will hit
Postgres `42P01` (`relation "agent_executions" does not exist`) on
its INSERT. The writer catches this exact code and logs at DEBUG.
Do NOT escalate to WARN/ERROR until migration 030 is present in
`schema_migrations` — operators tail logs during rollout and a 503-
class error during this window is a known-tolerable state.

Until migration 030 has applied, admin cost endpoints (`/admin/cost/*`)
return `{ available: false, reason: "migration_pending" }` with HTTP
200. They do not 500. This matches the precedent in admin `/audit-log`
which catches `42P01` and returns `entries: []` with a `notice`.

### I-7. Backfill from `model_log` is one-shot and idempotent

`backend/scripts/backfill-cost-from-model-log.ts` reads
`research_runs.model_log` JSONB for runs since a `--since` flag (default:
beginning of the year) and inserts `agent_executions` rows using the
same idempotency key. Re-running the script is safe — it is a no-op for
rows already inserted. The script does NOT write to `model_log` (read
only).

The backfill cannot perfectly reconstruct `started_at_ms` for historical
rows because `model_log` only stores `durationMs`. We use
`research_runs.completed_at - (cumulative duration up to this row)` as
a best-effort approximation, ordered by index in the array. Document
this lossiness in the backfill output.

### I-8. RLS does not apply to `agent_executions`

`agent_executions` is admin-only data. The table is created without
RLS enabled. Admin endpoints use `adminQuery` (same as `audit_log`,
`telemetry/runs`). User-facing endpoints **must never** query this
table; if a user wants their own cost data, expose a sanitized
read-only view in a future WO, never the raw table.

### I-9. Phase ≠ Role

The Cost Sidecar spec mixes "phase" (Planner / Discovery / Retriever /
Reasoner / Skeptic / Synthesizer / Verifier / Report / Persistence)
with "role" (planner, retriever, reasoner, skeptic, synthesizer,
verifier, plain_language_synthesizer, outline_architect, section_drafter,
internal_challenger, coherence_refiner, revision_intake, report_locator,
change_planner, section_rewriter, citation_integrity_checker,
final_revision_verifier).

`agent_executions.agent_role` stores the **role** (canonical, stable,
machine-grade — `REASONING_MODEL_ROLES` in `reasoningModelPolicy.ts`).
`agent_executions.phase` stores the **phase** (human-grouped pipeline
stage). Compute the phase from `(role, call_purpose)` in the writer
using a fixed mapping in `costSidecar.ts:rolePhaseFor()`. Do not let
phase drift from role — if you add a new role, add its phase mapping
in the same commit.

### I-10. Tests must fail without the fix (Cursor rule 16)

Every assertion in `costSidecar.test.ts` and `costSidecarApi.test.ts`
must fail when the relevant production code is reverted. Specifically:

- The idempotency test must insert the same (run_id, role, ts, model)
  twice and assert exactly 1 row exists. Mentally revert the
  `ON CONFLICT` clause — the test must fail.
- The deploy-skew test must drop the `agent_executions` table and
  assert the emit path neither throws nor produces a 500. Mentally
  revert the 42P01 catch — the test must fail.
- The price=0 test must call with a model not in `model_pricing` and
  assert the row exists with tokens but `calculated_cost_usd=0`.

## Pre-commit check

- [ ] No new `emitCallTelemetry` call sites outside `openrouterService.ts`.
- [ ] No `await` added to the emit path (it stays fire-and-forget).
- [ ] If you added a new `ReasoningModelRole`, you added its phase
      mapping in `costSidecar.ts:rolePhaseFor` in the same commit.
- [ ] If you renamed a column on `agent_executions`, you grepped
      every reader (admin routes, frontend, backfill script) per
      Cursor rule 17.
- [ ] If the migration adds an index or constraint, it is wrapped in
      `IF NOT EXISTS` per Cursor rule 13.
